Project Planning Phase
egalease – Project Planning Phase

The Project Planning Phase is the first major stage of developing the Legalease project. It focuses on defining the project objectives, scope, requirements, resources, timeline, and development strategy before actual implementation begins.

1. Project Objective

The main objective of Legalease is to develop a user-friendly legal information platform that helps people understand basic legal information, find relevant resources, and prepare simple legal documents.

2. Project Scope

The project will focus on:

Providing general legal information.
Allowing users to search legal topics.
Providing an AI-assisted question-and-answer feature.
Categorizing common legal issues.
Providing basic document templates.
Connecting users with relevant official resources.
Providing a simple and accessible user interface.

The system is intended for general legal information, not as a replacement for qualified legal professionals.

3. Requirement Planning
Functional Requirements

The system should provide:

User registration and login.
Legal information search.
AI legal assistant.
Legal issue categorization.
Document templates.
Document generation.
Official resource links.
Query history.
Admin management.
Non-Functional Requirements

The system should be:

User-friendly
Secure
Reliable
Responsive
Scalable
Easy to maintain
Fast in processing user requests
