10. Expected Outcome

At the end of the planning phase, the team should have:

Clearly defined project objectives.
Identified user requirements.
Defined project scope.
Selected suitable technologies.
Allocated responsibilities.
Prepared a development schedule.
Identified risks and solutions.
Established measurable project milestones.
11. Conclusion

The Project Planning Phase provides the foundation for the entire Legalease project. Proper planning ensures that the development team understands what needs to be built, how it will be built, what resources are required, and when each stage should be completed. This helps the project proceed systematically through ideation, design, development, demonstration, testing, and documentation.
